From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:07:11 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 71/97] Plutonium: tabs' web notifications and the host's color
 scheme in the Plutonium domain

Web notifications (new Notification(), a service worker's showNotification())
go to Ash's message center, which shell mode never shows. The Plutonium
DevTools domain now lists the web pages' ones there (PlutoniumWebNotifications,
a message center observer): notificationShown (each there is on enable, then
new and updated ones; the site's origin, title, body, a PNG data URL icon,
button labels) and notificationClosed. notificationAction clicks one or one of
its buttons, or closes it, through the message center, so Chrome's own
handling runs: the page's onclick, the worker's notificationclick. The
helper's notifications service shows them.

setColorScheme sets Ash's dark mode (the user's ash.dark_mode.enabled pref),
which the color palette controller carries to the web's native theme: the
helper follows the host's color scheme (the settings portal) with it, so
prefers-color-scheme in shells and tabs is the desktop's.
